  "body": {
    "id": "prop:single-donor-reduction",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "Let \\(P_0\\in\\mathcal M_I\\) satisfy the strict theorem-point conditions\n\\[\n p_X(x)>\\kappa_0,quad \\epsilon_0<p_g(x)<1-\\epsilon_0,quad\n \\max_{g,t}E_{P_{0,O}}[|Y_t|^4\\mid G=g]<M_4,quad\n \\lambda_{\\min}\\{B(x)^{\\prime}B(x)\\}>\\kappa_0\n\\]\nin every stratum and group, with every positive eigenvalue of \\(\\Omega_x\\) strictly larger than \\(\\kappa_0\\) and \\(\\operatorname{rank}(\\Omega_x)\\) locally constant at \\(P_0\\). When \\(J=1\\), \\(A_{\\mathrm{PT}}=0\\), so profiling the sole treated-versus-donor equality leaves no PT observed-data normal and the PT observed-law tangent space is unrestricted. At this intersection law the full-rank SC observed model is locally nested in the PT observed model, \\(\\mathcal I_{\\mathrm{PT}}(P_0)\\subseteq\\mathcal I_{\\mathrm{SC}}(P_0)\\), \\(\\phi_U=\\phi_{\\mathrm{PT}}\\), and \\(V_U=V_{\\mathrm{PT}}\\). With \\(T=2\\), this PT gradient equals the panel-DiD ATT efficient influence function in SantAnnaZhao2020, Proposition 1(a), equation (2.11), whose efficiency bound is equation (2.12).",
